    "done_when": "Inputs: the attribution at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cco-fixed-point-attribution.md section 3. Reuse the existing pair-builder arguments in scripts/analytic_oracle_fixtures/centroid_row.py and the existing receipt driver; change no solver code and no tolerance. In benchmarks/centroid_constrained_fixture_receipt.py: set field_scale_t to the 0.25 T declared bound, pass initial_level_wb as the level target minus the seed's reading at the level point, and write the newton_krylov history fields (per-step relative residual, achieved Krylov residual and tolerance, backtrack and promotion counts) into the receipt. Then one three-column positive-control receipt on the weak-rotation-reactor-static -110 fixture (135 realised cells), exact clip, the same 20 mm displaced seed (digest 062b465a7364914f), with the solver budget unchanged at 10 Newton steps and 30 GMRES iterations. GPU rung 1 is a real betelgeuse submission (gpu_0003_grpA, --gres=gpu:1, 8 CPUs, --mem=128G, TMPDIR=/tmp in submit and payload, the shared interpreter run directly, never uv on the node). Rung 2 is titan (--partition=titan --gres=gpu:1), used only if the betelgeuse job is still PENDING on a resource reason a minute after submission. Never decide from a --test-only estimate. You are authorised to submit this one job; the host line against srun, sbatch and salloc means do not nest work on the fleet node. Write the manifest with the job id and a declared wait before waiting. The receipt and its poloidal contour panel (plotting rules: wall, both null sets, analytic contours on shared levels; SVG beside PNG) land under docs/figures/centroid-constrained-oracle-solve/unit-leverage/. The report at /home/ITER/mcintos/.config/reckon/crew/reports/nova/s22/cco-unit-leverage-positive-control.md states the verdict against the attribution's rules: confirmed if the terminal residual and both rows' scaled residuals reach at most 1e-12 with superlinear decrease over the final